spans.s:
प्र-वाचन, अम्, n. a proclamation, promulgation;
a designation; द्वि-प्रवाचन, having a twofold
designation.

प्रावण प्रावण, अस्, अम्, m. n. (according
to Sāy.) a spade, shovel; (either a lengthened form
for प्र-वण or a derivative from it.)

प्रवह्लि प्र-वह्लि, इस्, or प्र-वह्ली, or प्र-
वह्लिका, f. a riddle, enigma, conundrum, charade;
[cf. प्र-वल्ह, प्रवल्हिका.]

प्र-वर्षण, अम्, n. raining, causing to rain;
the first rain; N. of the twenty-third Adhyāya of
the Bṛhat-saṃhitā of Varāha-mihira.

प्रवे प्र-वे, cl. 1. P. A. -वयति, -ते, -वातुम्,
to sew lengthwise [cf. प्रोत]; to pierce, transfix;
to infix, impale.

प्रवेक प्र-वेक, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. विच् with
प्र), choicest, most excellent, best, principal, chief;
(at the end of a comp., cf. मणि-प्˚.)

प्र-वेपन, अस्, m., N. of a serpent-demon;
(अम्), n. trembling, tremulous motion, shaking,
agitation; (also wrongly spelt प्र-वेपण.)

प्रव्याहृ प्र-व्य्-आ-हृ, cl. 1. P. A. -हरति,
-ते, -हर्तुम्, to declare beforehand, foretell, predict;
to howl, yell, roar.

प्रावाहणि प्रावाहणि, इस्, m. a patronymic
from Pra-vāhaṇa; (also wrongly written प्राहणि,
प्रावहणि.)
